WEBVTT

00:00.370 --> 00:01.170
Lico—

00:14.270 --> 00:19.290
<i>This is the tale of a genius patissier 
who died before his time,</i>

00:19.290 --> 00:23.290
<i>and was reincarnated as the son 
of a poor noble in another world</i>

00:23.630 --> 00:26.670
<i>to pursue a world full 
of desserts and smiles.</i>

00:27.550 --> 00:32.250
<i>It's a tale that is at once cold 
and unsparing, and syrupy sweet.</i>

00:33.710 --> 00:40.090
<i>His dream is to create this 
world's very own land of sweets!</i>

00:48.060 --> 00:50.650
<b>Sweet Reincarnation</b>

02:12.880 --> 02:18.220
<b>Apples of Love and Sad Threats of War</b>

02:19.220 --> 02:20.360
Licorice!

02:22.590 --> 02:23.580
Milady?!

02:23.580 --> 02:24.790
Licorice!

02:25.540 --> 02:27.300
L-Lord Pastry!

02:27.970 --> 02:30.960
Wh-What in the world were you...

02:31.210 --> 02:33.090
I'll explain later.

02:33.090 --> 02:34.840
Leave this to me!

02:35.700 --> 02:38.880
Well, well! Hasn't this become amusing?

02:39.650 --> 02:40.810
<i>Licorice!</i>

02:48.770 --> 02:49.800
Licorice!

02:58.760 --> 03:00.080
I'm sorry.

03:01.680 --> 03:05.030
I'm sorry... Pastry.

03:05.360 --> 03:08.500
L-Listen. Count Retes was just...

03:10.500 --> 03:14.210
Look, she just sees me as a 9-year-old ki—

03:14.210 --> 03:15.860
It's not just that.

03:17.170 --> 03:22.550
In the great hall... everyone was...
 talking about you.

03:23.220 --> 03:25.520
All those women...

03:25.870 --> 03:28.140
And hearing them like that...

03:29.720 --> 03:33.190
I began to imagine the most awful things.

03:33.190 --> 03:34.610
Awful things?

03:34.610 --> 03:41.210
If someone else were to express 
their fondness for you...

03:42.530 --> 03:45.080
Then maybe... you wouldn't...

03:46.160 --> 03:49.500
You wouldn't want me anymore.

03:49.500 --> 03:51.460
I would never—

03:52.870 --> 03:55.420
My sister, Petra...

03:55.920 --> 04:00.740
She can talk with anyone so easily.

04:01.140 --> 04:04.950
She can be so bold. Everyone likes her.

04:05.450 --> 04:07.720
By comparison, I...

04:09.530 --> 04:12.850
If only I were more like her.

04:15.280 --> 04:17.150
Even if you have trouble talking,

04:17.150 --> 04:18.650
and even if you're reserved,

04:19.000 --> 04:21.030
that's just part of who you are.

04:23.080 --> 04:26.700
You don't have to be Lady Petra.

04:28.110 --> 04:31.210
I like you just the way you are.

04:32.810 --> 04:37.630
And I'm sure I'll only come 
to like you even more.

04:39.570 --> 04:44.980
Will you trust me, 
and believe what I'm saying?

04:46.920 --> 04:48.000
Yes...

04:50.120 --> 04:51.780
Could you wait a minute?

04:53.610 --> 04:55.850
Please, just wait here.

04:56.210 --> 04:58.800
Trust me, no matter what.

05:02.950 --> 05:04.130
Please.

05:37.800 --> 05:39.520
Sorry to keep you waiting!

05:40.030 --> 05:41.060
That's all right.

05:48.430 --> 05:51.450
Is this... like before?

05:51.730 --> 05:52.680
Yes.

05:52.680 --> 05:55.410
But it's not quite like the one from before.

05:56.750 --> 05:58.620
I made this for you.

05:58.890 --> 06:01.880
A fresh, special one, just for you.

06:03.040 --> 06:04.790
Would you do me the honor of accepting it?

06:12.710 --> 06:16.650
I... I'd really like you to eat it.

06:18.540 --> 06:21.190
I made it just for you, after all.

06:36.520 --> 06:39.640
<i>The aroma of the fruit, and the sweetness...</i>

06:39.640 --> 06:42.080
<i>They're filling my mouth.</i>

06:43.130 --> 06:46.850
<i>The taste of happiness 
I shared alone with Pastry...</i>

06:47.240 --> 06:49.050
<i>Just for us.</i>

06:50.200 --> 06:56.200
<i>No one else. Just me and him...</i>

07:01.350 --> 07:03.860
R-Really, it's not...

07:04.260 --> 07:06.300
I'm not crying from sadness.

07:11.310 --> 07:12.890
It's delicious.

07:14.090 --> 07:15.310
Hey, Licorice.

07:15.690 --> 07:19.960
I know this treat by the name "candy apple."

07:19.960 --> 07:22.040
Candy... apple?

07:22.250 --> 07:25.070
But there are other names for it.

07:25.070 --> 07:26.300
Other names?

07:27.130 --> 07:30.540
It's very simple to make,

07:30.540 --> 07:32.970
so it's made in many places,

07:33.450 --> 07:37.560
and has come to have just as many names.

07:38.310 --> 07:39.710
Toffee apple.

07:40.310 --> 07:41.850
Heaven's apple.

07:42.710 --> 07:44.370
Apple of paradise.

07:44.370 --> 07:45.290
And...

07:47.280 --> 07:49.170
apple of love.

07:53.670 --> 07:55.510
My feelings for you are unwavering,

07:55.510 --> 07:58.580
and I've poured them all into this treat.

08:02.480 --> 08:03.500
Please...

08:04.330 --> 08:05.500
Licorice.

08:05.730 --> 08:08.460
Will you trust me?

08:10.730 --> 08:14.310
I... I want to make you happy.

08:14.920 --> 08:16.140
I want to make you smile.

08:18.610 --> 08:21.000
I want nothing more than to see your smile...

08:22.020 --> 08:23.190
Licorice.

08:28.740 --> 08:29.900
It's delicious!

08:30.220 --> 08:31.860
Licorice!

08:32.510 --> 08:35.320
Thank you, Pastry!

08:35.770 --> 08:38.540
And... I'm sorry.

08:39.310 --> 08:41.220
<i>Such a beautiful smile...</i>

08:41.770 --> 08:44.500
<i>I came this close to losing it.</i>

08:45.750 --> 08:48.790
<i>My dream is to create a land of sweets,</i>

08:48.790 --> 08:51.900
<i>and bring smiles to the faces 
of everyone in this world.</i>

08:52.730 --> 08:56.960
<i>I can't do that if I can't at least 
bring smiles to the people I care about.</i>

08:58.220 --> 09:00.410
<i>I'll make it together with Licorice.</i>

09:00.900 --> 09:02.430
<i>A land of sweets...</i>

09:05.850 --> 09:08.580
We came to fetch you, milady.

09:08.580 --> 09:10.560
I saw you, Young Master!

09:10.560 --> 09:11.610
Great work!

09:11.610 --> 09:14.530
Nicolo... how long were you watching?

09:14.530 --> 09:16.780
How long?

09:16.780 --> 09:17.690
Oh, right.

09:17.690 --> 09:20.240
Since you came back with 
that "apple of love" thing!

09:21.520 --> 09:24.840
Whoo, there's the loverboy 
everyone's talking about!

09:24.840 --> 09:26.630
The Fief of Morteln's own gigolo!

09:26.630 --> 09:28.630
Ladykiller!

09:28.630 --> 09:30.490
Is that right?

09:30.490 --> 09:31.500
Nicolo...

09:32.180 --> 09:35.790
You seem eager for more work lately.

09:36.970 --> 09:41.050
So when we get back home, 
I'll double your workload!

09:41.050 --> 09:43.980
U-Um, Young Master... you're scaring me.

09:44.310 --> 09:47.190
You're joking about the 
doubled workload, right?

09:47.600 --> 09:51.520
Really? Double sounds like a joke, does it?

09:51.780 --> 09:53.980
I'll triple it, then!

09:53.980 --> 09:56.030
Forgive me!

09:56.030 --> 09:59.820
I won't tell your father, 
so please, forgive me!

10:00.500 --> 10:02.840
Your good spirits seem to be restored.

10:07.880 --> 10:09.580
She's burning holes in my back.

10:11.690 --> 10:13.670
Pas, my love!

10:13.670 --> 10:15.380
Welcome home!

10:17.730 --> 10:21.050
I'm back... M-Mother.

10:22.620 --> 10:24.510
Did you enjoy the tea tasting ceremony?

10:24.740 --> 10:27.230
Good work on your first diplomatic mission.

10:29.190 --> 10:32.080
I-I can't breathe, Mother!

10:32.080 --> 10:34.660
Come, Agnes. Release the boy.

10:34.660 --> 10:36.400
I really think you're choking him.

10:37.220 --> 10:39.110
I've returned.

10:39.690 --> 10:41.000
Welcome home.

10:43.590 --> 10:44.790
Is something...

10:45.070 --> 10:48.520
Pas zapped himself back here this afternoon

10:48.520 --> 10:51.710
and busied himself with something-or-other...

10:52.420 --> 10:56.110
Could it have been something 
for you, my dear?

10:56.110 --> 10:56.900
<i>Erk!</i>

10:59.580 --> 11:05.220
I'd <i>love</i> to hear <i>all</i> about what happened!

11:05.220 --> 11:06.850
Pas, dear!

11:08.030 --> 11:09.870
Please, be gentle!

11:11.610 --> 11:16.020
She might be more intimidating 
than the count...

11:25.210 --> 11:27.990
I... I'm exhausted.

11:30.690 --> 11:34.630
You had to humor the mistress 
for two straight hours, eh?

11:34.630 --> 11:35.810
Well done.

11:35.810 --> 11:37.930
Want some bean tea?

11:38.280 --> 11:39.630
Sure, thanks.

11:43.220 --> 11:44.220
Help yourself!

11:44.220 --> 11:46.310
Thanks so much...

11:46.310 --> 11:47.910
<b>Slurp</b>

11:49.860 --> 11:51.020
That's so good!

11:51.790 --> 11:53.230
What's all this here?

11:55.450 --> 11:59.400
Oh, that's leftover wrapping 
paper for the hard candy.

11:59.830 --> 12:04.580
Mother and I wrapped them as I humored her.

12:05.240 --> 12:07.290
Wrapping paper for the hard candy?

12:07.290 --> 12:07.870
Wait...

12:08.180 --> 12:09.830
What in the world is this?

12:10.120 --> 12:11.910
It's just what it looks like.

12:13.260 --> 12:15.220
You used this as wrapping paper?

12:15.220 --> 12:17.250
What were you thinking?

12:17.880 --> 12:21.240
Revenge for her messing with me and Licorice.

12:21.240 --> 12:22.220
A minor thing.

12:24.570 --> 12:27.350
How dare he! That awful child!

12:28.780 --> 12:31.340
P-Please remain calm, Your Ladyship!

12:32.620 --> 12:36.480
He sent candy to all the 
nobles wrapped in that paper!

12:36.480 --> 12:37.490
And because of that...

12:37.490 --> 12:43.150
People are spreading rumors 
that I "like them young"!

12:43.580 --> 12:44.930
And ever since,

12:44.930 --> 12:50.290
we've been receiving dozens of offers 
every day from far-too-young prospects...

12:50.290 --> 12:52.370
This one's eight years old.

12:52.870 --> 12:55.310
This one's ten years old.

12:55.310 --> 12:57.830
He's completely gumming up the works!

12:58.860 --> 13:02.050
You'll pay for this, child!

13:02.690 --> 13:07.720
<b>Estate of Margrave Hubarek</b>

13:03.820 --> 13:08.010
My lord, there are stirrings 
from Margrave Lutoroute.

13:09.370 --> 13:12.360
As expected, he'll be making 
his move before the summer.

13:12.890 --> 13:16.660
He seems to have realized that 
the union between our house

13:17.090 --> 13:19.110
and Duke Kadlecek's would strengthen our army.

13:19.110 --> 13:21.240
And he's decided to invade before then.

13:22.250 --> 13:25.930
Hence his earlier aggressions?

13:26.490 --> 13:29.120
It sounds like something Lutoroute would do.

13:29.950 --> 13:35.080
He seems eager to conclude 
your long rivalry at last.

13:35.080 --> 13:37.510
So? What's the scale of his army?

13:37.510 --> 13:40.040
Reports say it's almost 
thirty thousand strong.

13:40.730 --> 13:42.410
Thirty thousand, eh?

13:42.410 --> 13:47.010
I can't say we're prepared to 
defend against a force that large.

13:47.540 --> 13:50.720
Send a messenger to Duke Kadlecek 
in the royal capital at once.

13:51.210 --> 13:53.500
I'll compose a letter 
requesting reinforcements.

13:53.500 --> 13:54.260
Milord.

13:58.330 --> 14:00.060
Damn you, Lutoroute.

14:01.370 --> 14:04.390
Chu, chu, takokai na...

14:04.390 --> 14:07.320
Chu, chu, takokai na...

14:07.590 --> 14:10.910
Kid? What's that weird little chant?

14:11.410 --> 14:13.450
It's a kind of counting song.

14:14.050 --> 14:15.690
The profits from the hard candy

14:15.690 --> 14:17.370
plus the matchmaking photos

14:17.700 --> 14:20.950
total up to 384 coins!

14:20.950 --> 14:24.800
Hey! You reached your target!

14:24.800 --> 14:25.800
Yes!

14:26.200 --> 14:30.720
The silvers and these four extra 
leftover golds will go into my savings.

14:31.020 --> 14:34.680
That's an awfully high amount 
for someone your age.

14:35.350 --> 14:39.390
Appropriate recompense for 
my time making sweets!

14:40.060 --> 14:44.610
Well, you earned us a profit, 
so I doubt the boss will complain.

14:45.070 --> 14:47.440
Well, will you be using 
it for what you expected?

14:48.410 --> 14:53.780
Yes, ask the traveling merchant 
to round up a hundred goats!

14:54.150 --> 14:54.910
What?

14:54.910 --> 14:58.000
Earlier, you said you'd want 70 or 80...

14:58.350 --> 15:00.950
We'll overbid for a hundred,

15:00.950 --> 15:03.960
then probably end up 
compromising at 70 to 80.

15:04.230 --> 15:06.000
That's dirty business.

15:06.000 --> 15:10.590
See if you can get him to 
throw in three donkeys!

15:10.590 --> 15:12.260
You better rein it in a little.

15:12.260 --> 15:14.300
You're gonna make the merchant cry.

15:14.550 --> 15:17.940
Goat milk and cheese are amazing!

15:17.940 --> 15:20.600
They're just perfect for use in sweets!

15:22.860 --> 15:24.520
What will I make?

15:25.170 --> 15:26.950
Goats, huh?

15:26.950 --> 15:31.170
We tried to raise those 
in our early days here.

15:32.520 --> 15:34.150
Father told me about it.

15:34.530 --> 15:37.930
Goats will eat anything, 
so they're easy to raise.

15:38.460 --> 15:39.490
Yeah.

15:40.140 --> 15:43.070
But since they'll eat anything...

15:43.450 --> 15:45.370
With our land barren enough as it was,

15:45.370 --> 15:49.570
we couldn't afford to hold them,
and the boss let them go.

15:50.850 --> 15:53.040
But now the land's rich and green!

15:54.550 --> 15:56.390
Now I can start adding more livestock,

15:56.390 --> 15:58.970
and take another step 
toward my land of sweets!

15:59.330 --> 16:04.190
So will we be eating the chickens now?

16:04.190 --> 16:05.710
Don't be ridiculous!

16:05.710 --> 16:06.650
Wh-What?!

16:06.650 --> 16:10.080
Chickens are absolutely essential!

16:10.840 --> 16:12.820
If anything, we'll need <i>more</i> of them!

16:13.140 --> 16:16.090
Cakes, cookies, custards, meringue!

16:16.090 --> 16:18.160
We need eggs for all of them!

16:18.440 --> 16:21.590
We <i>cannot</i> be a fief without eggs!

16:21.590 --> 16:24.120
So it's the sweets we're 
worried about, right?

16:24.330 --> 16:26.840
But in that case...

16:27.360 --> 16:29.800
The lack of workers might be an issue.

16:29.800 --> 16:33.920
I'll need to mull that one over.

16:33.920 --> 16:35.280
Let's take a breather!

16:39.370 --> 16:40.440
Feuille...

16:40.440 --> 16:42.580
Would you take a taste of this?

16:45.420 --> 16:46.980
What's this stuff?

16:47.290 --> 16:53.450
It's extracted from sweet sorghum, 
a particular kind of sorghum grass.

16:56.260 --> 16:58.620
Seems pretty sticky...

16:58.920 --> 17:02.110
I tried to boil it down a bit to thicken it,

17:02.110 --> 17:03.790
but it didn't really work.

17:03.790 --> 17:06.330
Still, that shouldn't affect flavor.

17:07.690 --> 17:08.540
That's sweet!

17:08.780 --> 17:10.980
It's incredibly sweet!

17:10.980 --> 17:13.000
It's a first experiment in making sugar.

17:13.000 --> 17:14.010
Sugar?

17:14.350 --> 17:19.220
I'll improve the recipe and turn Morteln 
into a producer of confectioneries!

17:19.430 --> 17:23.110
If I can just produce my own sugar, 
I can produce as many desserts as I—

17:23.110 --> 17:24.850
If you say so.

17:25.940 --> 17:29.440
Just don't use your magic, 
or the boss might smite you again.

17:30.200 --> 17:32.450
I swear, I've learned my lesson!

17:43.900 --> 17:45.830
What are you doing?

17:45.830 --> 17:48.290
We're making a juicer!

17:48.500 --> 17:50.360
A juicer?

17:51.940 --> 17:53.920
Yes, it's done!

17:56.040 --> 17:57.680
I'll show you.

17:59.710 --> 18:02.350
We've placed sorghum 
grass stalks in the cask,

18:02.350 --> 18:06.020
and we're going to extract juice from them.

18:06.020 --> 18:07.380
Hey!

18:07.940 --> 18:10.220
I can't reach it!

18:10.220 --> 18:12.020
You're so short, Marc.

18:12.280 --> 18:14.990
Shut up! You're shorter than I am!

18:15.920 --> 18:18.240
Maybe I messed up the measurements...

18:18.240 --> 18:20.720
Fine. Get on, Lumi!

18:20.720 --> 18:21.700
Okay!

18:25.460 --> 18:28.610
Lumi, go slow so that it doesn't break!

18:31.250 --> 18:33.750
You're heavy, damn it!

18:34.120 --> 18:35.300
What was that?!

18:35.300 --> 18:36.970
You wanna fight, you jerk?

18:36.970 --> 18:38.490
Please don't fight!

18:38.490 --> 18:40.430
Keep pulling it, slowly!

18:40.760 --> 18:41.890
Got it!

18:42.210 --> 18:44.210
You're so heavy!

18:44.210 --> 18:46.470
There you go again!

18:46.470 --> 18:47.930
Lumi, no!

18:50.870 --> 18:51.810
Look out!

18:55.530 --> 18:57.440
A-Are you all right?

18:57.740 --> 18:59.280
Was anyone hurt?

18:59.530 --> 19:00.490
Ow...

19:00.490 --> 19:02.140
I-I'm okay.

19:02.140 --> 19:03.910
Damn it...

19:05.510 --> 19:08.620
I guess it won't be that easy.

19:09.170 --> 19:11.580
I think I got the idea right,

19:11.860 --> 19:14.520
but it's just not tough enough...

19:14.840 --> 19:17.550
Maybe I should make it all from iron?

19:17.550 --> 19:19.760
That might work, but...

19:22.730 --> 19:24.740
If you have an idea, tell me.

19:24.740 --> 19:28.220
The purpose of a prototype 
is to be improved upon.

19:30.240 --> 19:35.520
In sweets, too, you can only make something 
good after trial, error, and improvement.

19:36.030 --> 19:39.990
Trial and error are essential 
to producing sweets!

19:40.280 --> 19:42.950
You make a thousand good 
sweets by making one first!

19:43.710 --> 19:46.010
You know what he's talking about?

19:46.010 --> 19:47.160
No idea.

19:47.640 --> 19:50.680
I don't have the diagram or anything...

19:50.680 --> 19:53.950
But in Hubarek, when they make wine,

19:53.950 --> 19:57.880
they use something like your juicer there.

19:59.090 --> 20:04.550
<b>Squeeze</b>

19:59.400 --> 20:03.720
I think it involves two 
people turning a lever...

20:05.070 --> 20:07.760
Wine? That might just do it!

20:08.430 --> 20:09.720
I see!

20:09.720 --> 20:12.100
If a tool for that purpose already exists,

20:12.600 --> 20:15.010
let's figure out a way to get one!

20:15.010 --> 20:17.690
That'll reduce mistakes!

20:17.930 --> 20:19.690
Thanks, Licorice!

20:20.730 --> 20:21.650
It was nothing.

20:22.180 --> 20:27.370
What was all that crap about 
trial and error, then?

20:27.370 --> 20:28.640
Sheesh.

20:28.640 --> 20:31.120
You made me fall on my butt for no reason.

20:31.480 --> 20:34.330
I'll ask you to be my taste-tester, then.

20:36.470 --> 20:37.790
I forgive you!

20:37.790 --> 20:39.420
You never change.

20:40.730 --> 20:42.470
Time is money!

20:42.810 --> 20:46.300
I'm gonna get back and talk 
to Feuille about the juicer!

20:47.310 --> 20:50.010
Sorry, can you guys clean up for me here?

20:50.390 --> 20:51.720
You got it!

20:54.040 --> 20:56.650
Pas is having so much fun...

20:56.650 --> 21:00.510
Sugar, goat milk, fresh eggs,

21:00.510 --> 21:04.490
cheese, flour, yogurt!

21:04.860 --> 21:06.820
I'm so excited!

21:06.820 --> 21:09.280
What dessert will I make first?

21:09.550 --> 21:11.740
I'm gonna bake my heart out!

21:12.090 --> 21:15.960
A cake? No, maybe I'll try flan?

21:16.190 --> 21:19.050
Choux a la creme, maybe?!

21:24.380 --> 21:26.800
Father! You're back?

21:29.120 --> 21:33.220
How were Duke Kadlecek and Lord Squale?

21:36.570 --> 21:37.650
Father?

21:38.030 --> 21:42.130
Kid... we've got bad news.

21:42.650 --> 21:44.570
What is it?

21:46.010 --> 21:48.030
War has begun.

21:49.990 --> 21:55.740
It started between Hubarek's lands in 
the east and their neighbor, Lutoroute.

22:01.140 --> 22:02.700
<i>War?</i>

23:37.060 --> 23:38.990
Next time on <i>Sweet Reincarnation</i>...

23:39.120 --> 23:45.020
<b>Reinforcements and a Bittersweet First Deployment</b>

23:39.420 --> 23:41.540
"Reinforcements and a 
Bittersweet First Deployment."

23:41.860 --> 23:43.250
Bon appétit!

23:45.020 --> 23:50.250
<b>Illustration:</b>

23:45.020 --> 23:50.250
<b>Ren Hidoh</b>
